 "stem": "When the polynomial $A$ is divided by $x+{=p}$, the quotient is $x+{=q}$ and the remainder is ${=r}$. Find the polynomial $A$.",
 "answer": "",
 "solution": [
  "Here $B=x+{=p}$, $Q=x+{=q}$ and $R={=r}$.",
  "Write $A=BQ+R$: $A=(x+{=p})(x+{=q})+{=r}$.",
  "Multiply: $(x+{=p})(x+{=q})=x^2+{=q}x+{=p}x+{=p*q}=x^2+{=p+q}x+{=p*q}$.",
  "Add the remainder: $x^2+{=p+q}x+{=p*q}+{=r}$.",
  "So $A=x^2+{=p+q}x+{=p*q+r}$."
 ],
